{"title":"Career Roadmap · Immunohaematology Technician","role":"Immunohaematology Technician","summary":"An Immunohaematology Technician works in blood banks, transfusion services and clinical laboratories, focusing on the relationship between blood group antigens, antibodies and transfusion compatibility.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Blood Banking Technology / Transfusion Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Immunohaematology Technician works in blood banks, transfusion services and clinical laboratories, focusing on the relationship between blood group antigens, antibodies and transfusion compatibility."},{"type":"p","text":"The role typically involves:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ABO and Rh blood grouping"},{"text":"Antibody screening"},{"text":"Antibody identification"},{"text":"Crossmatching"},{"text":"Compatibility testing"},{"text":"Direct/indirect antiglobulin testing"},{"text":"Investigation of transfusion reactions"},{"text":"Blood-component testing"},{"text":"Donor and recipient sample processing"},{"text":"Quality control"},{"text":"Documentation and traceability"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The role is particularly important because an error in blood-group or compatibility testing can have serious consequences. Therefore, accuracy, documentation, quality systems and adherence to approved laboratory procedures are essential."},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification note","text":"The exact eligibility and permitted scope for an “Immunohaematology Technician” can vary by institution and Indian state/employer. Students should choose a recognized laboratory/blood-bank/transfusion-technology qualification with appropriate clinical laboratory training and verify current recruitment and regulatory requirements."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Class 12 – PCB / Relevant Eligibility","B.Sc / Allied Health / Medical Laboratory /"]},{"type":"flow","items":["Blood Bank / Transfusion Technology Program","Clinical Laboratory & Blood Bank Training","Blood Bank Internship","Blood Bank / Transfusion Service Technician","Immunohaematology Technician","Senior Immunohaematology / Blood Bank Technologist","Specialized Transfusion Service / Quality / Reference Laboratory","Senior Technical / Supervisory / Application / Research Roles"]}]},{"heading":"What You Learn During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Biological & Laboratory Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a strong foundation in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy"},{"text":"Human physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Cell biology"},{"text":"Genetics"},{"text":"Pathology"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Basic laboratory safety"},{"text":"Biosafety"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Laboratory ethics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Key objective"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the cellular, genetic and biochemical basis of blood and immune reactions."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Hematology & Immunology"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop knowledge of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Hematology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"RBCs"},{"text":"WBCs"},{"text":"Platelets"},{"text":"Hemoglobin"},{"text":"Hematopoiesis"},{"text":"Blood disorders"},{"text":"Peripheral blood examination"},{"text":"Hemolysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Immunology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Antigens"},{"text":"Antibodies"},{"text":"Immune responses"},{"text":"Complement"},{"text":"Antigen-antibody reactions"},{"text":"Autoantibodies"},{"text":"Alloantibodies"},{"text":"Hypersensitivity"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Blood grouping"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the principles behind:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ABO system"},{"text":"Rh system"},{"text":"Other clinically significant blood-group systems"},{"text":"Forward grouping"},{"text":"Reverse grouping"},{"text":"RhD testing"},{"text":"Weak/variant antigen concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Immunohaematology Specialization"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the core specialization stage."},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"h","text":"Compatibility testing"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ABO/Rh typing"},{"text":"Antibody screening"},{"text":"Antibody identification"},{"text":"Crossmatching"},{"text":"Compatibility testing"},{"text":"Antiglobulin testing"},{"text":"Direct antiglobulin test"},{"text":"Indirect antiglobulin test"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Antibody investigation"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinically significant antibodies"},{"text":"Alloantibodies"},{"text":"Autoantibodies"},{"text":"Antibody reactions"},{"text":"Reaction-strength interpretation"},{"text":"Temperature-dependent reactions"},{"text":"Dosage effects"},{"text":"Enzyme techniques"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Blood-group serology"},{"type":"p","text":"Gain exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rh antibodies"},{"text":"Kell"},{"text":"Kidd"},{"text":"Duffy"},{"text":"MNS"},{"text":"Other clinically significant blood-group systems"}]}]},{"heading":"Final Year — Blood Bank & Transfusion Practice","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop practical understanding of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Blood components"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Whole blood"},{"text":"Packed red blood cells"},{"text":"Fresh frozen plasma"},{"text":"Platelets"},{"text":"Cryoprecipitate"},{"text":"Specialized blood components"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Blood-bank operations"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Donor registration"},{"text":"Donor screening"},{"text":"Sample collection"},{"text":"Blood grouping"},{"text":"Component preparation"},{"text":"Storage"},{"text":"Inventory"},{"text":"Compatibility testing"},{"text":"Issue procedures"},{"text":"Traceability"},{"text":"Documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Transfusion safety"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Transfusion reactions"},{"text":"Clerical errors"},{"text":"Sample identification"},{"text":"Compatibility failures"},{"text":"Hemolytic reactions"},{"text":"Non-hemolytic reactions"},{"text":"Investigation procedures"},{"text":"Reporting and documentation"}]}]},{"heading":"Core Technical Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill","Target Level"],"rows":[[{"text":"Hematology"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Immunology"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Immunohaematology"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"ABO/Rh Typing"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Antibody Screening"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Antibody Identification"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Crossmatching"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"DAT/IAT"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Blood Component Knowledge"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Transfusion Reactions"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Blood-Bank Operations"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Quality Control"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Biosafety"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Laboratory Documentation"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"LIS / Laboratory IT"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Data Analysis"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Advanced"}]]}]},{"heading":"Immunohaematology Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A technician should understand the complete workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient / Donor Sample","Sample Identification","ABO & Rh Testing","Antibody Screening","Positive / Negative Result","If Positive → Antibody Investigation","Antibody Identification","Compatible Unit Selection","Crossmatching","Compatibility Assessment","Documentation & Traceability","Issue / Transfusion Service"]},{"type":"p","text":"Every stage requires strict adherence to the laboratory's approved SOPs."}]},{"heading":"Important Laboratory Techniques","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Gain supervised practical exposure to:"},{"type":"h","text":"Blood grouping"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tube methods"},{"text":"Gel/column agglutination"},{"text":"Automated blood-group testing where available"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Serological testing"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Agglutination techniques"},{"text":"Antiglobulin techniques"},{"text":"DAT"},{"text":"IAT"},{"text":"Antibody screening"},{"text":"Antibody identification panels"},{"text":"Crossmatching"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Sample processing"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Serum/plasma separation"},{"text":"RBC preparation"},{"text":"Sample labeling"},{"text":"Storage"},{"text":"Reagent handling"}]}]},{"heading":"Automated Blood-Bank Technology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Modern transfusion services increasingly use automation."},{"type":"p","text":"Become familiar with concepts behind:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Automated blood grouping"},{"text":"Automated crossmatching"},{"text":"Gel-card systems"},{"text":"Microcolumn technology"},{"text":"Immunohaematology analyzers"},{"text":"Blood-bank information systems"},{"text":"Barcode identification"},{"text":"Electronic traceability"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The goal is not merely operating one manufacturer's machine."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["sample","reagent","reaction","detection","interpretation","validation","documentation"]}]},{"heading":"Blood-Bank Quality Management","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Quality is one of the most important career differentiators."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SOP compliance"},{"text":"Internal quality control"},{"text":"Reagent quality checks"},{"text":"Equipment calibration/maintenance concepts"},{"text":"Temperature monitoring"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Non-conformance reporting"},{"text":"Corrective and preventive actions"},{"text":"Traceability"},{"text":"Internal audits"},{"text":"External quality as